  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study relies entirely on media representations in newspaper reports rather than direct observations of the regeneration projects or interviews with the actual participants.",
      "what": "This study analyzes a collection of newspaper reports on micro-regeneration projects in Shanghai using a narrative story arc framework. It identifies the structural elements of these media narratives to evaluate how different actor groups are portrayed as participating in and influencing the planning processes and outcomes.",
      "why": "It reveals how media narratives construct a story of 'constructive contestation,' showing how reports of local tensions are rhetorically used to emphasize consensus and collaboration as the dominant ethos of modern Chinese urban renewal."
